The advisory names only .end(). '(module)' is added conservatively: in 3.0.0 the main export runs the same /[
]+$/ regex (module.exports = string => string.replace(/^[
]+/, '').replace(/[
]+$/, '')), and 3.0.1 left it unchanged, so calling the main export may be just as slow. .start() uses only the anchored /^[
]+/ and is not included.
